## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Structured Investor Profiling (New Step Before Chat)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is the most impactful change. Instead of jumping straight into a chat, we guide the user through a structured profiling wizard that feeds context to the AI.

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/components/strategy/investor-profile-wizard.tsx`
A multi-step wizard (5 screens) that captures:

**Screen 1 — Investment Goal & Horizon**
- Primary objective: Capital Growth | Regular Income | Capital Preservation | Speculation
- Time horizon slider: 6 months → 1 year → 3 years → 5 years → 10+ years
- "When will you need this money?" — concrete date picker

**Screen 2 — Risk Tolerance (Behavioral)**
- Scenario-based questions instead of abstract "conservative/moderate/aggressive":
  - "If your portfolio dropped 20% in a month, you would:" → Sell everything / Sell some / Hold tight / Buy more
  - "Which portfolio would you prefer?" → Show two options with historical best/worst year ranges
  - "How often do you check your investments?" → Daily / Weekly / Monthly / Rarely
- These map to a computed risk score (1-10)

**Screen 3 — Capital & Existing Holdings**
- How much capital are you allocating to this strategy? (₹ amount or range)
- Do you already own stocks? → Yes (auto-detect from portfolio) / No
- If yes, show existing holdings and ask: "Should we avoid stocks you already own?"
- Monthly SIP amount (optional)

**Screen 4 — Preferences & Constraints**
- Sector preferences: Include/Exclude specific sectors (checkboxes with icons)
- Market cap preference: Large Cap / Mid Cap / Small Cap / All (visual slider)
- ESG/ethical constraints: Avoid tobacco, alcohol, gambling, etc.
- Dividend preference: Don't care / Prefer dividend-paying / Only dividend stocks

**Screen 5 — Experience Level**
- "How would you describe your investing experience?" → Beginner / Intermediate / Advanced
- This controls the **language complexity** of AI responses and whether to explain financial terms

